Small heads-up about the red `Code Blocks` check: it's a false positive, not something wrong with this PR. 🙂

The checker doesn't render Twig against a real Symfony app — it compiles it against a hardcoded whitelist in `symfony-tools/code-block-checker` (`src/Twig/DummyExtension.php`), and `access_decision()` / `access_decision_for_user()` are missing from it, hence `[Twig] Unknown "access_decision" function.`

It turns out 5 of the 8 functions registered by `SecurityExtension` are absent from that list, including `is_granted_for_user`, `impersonation_path` and `impersonation_url` — those are already documented here and only slip through because their code blocks predate the baseline. So any *new* Twig block documenting a security function hits this.

I opened symfony-tools/code-block-checker#57 to add the missing ones (green there). Once it's merged, re-running the CI here should turn this check green.

Also, thanks @MrYamous for the review — and for double-checking the types yourself before I even got to it. Reviewing your own review is next-level efficiency. 😄
